# A109 kernel desktop (sd-base, no #Z). The C:\ window is open at boot.
# Ticks are 200 Hz after "[desk] desktop up" armed the injector.
# A: idle — the C:\ window's info line (A109.3) and its frame.
# File title (88,8) -> F: the File box down (A109.1: 15 entries of 16 px =
# 240 tall, not 285). Out to the desktop, click = cancel, park -> H.
# Then the C:\ window's up arrow (580,96): press, drag the pointer away with
# the button still held (EmuTOS keeps the gadget SELECTED for the whole of
# `handle_arrow_msg`, gemctrl.c:272-284 — no leave tracking, unlike
# gr_watchbox), so the dump G shows the pressed cell without the cursor on
# it; release, park -> I.
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1400 move 88 8
1900 mark F_FILE_OPEN
2200 move 400 300
2500 down
2503 up
2800 parkbr
3200 mark H_MENU_CLOSED
3500 move 580 96
3700 down
3750 drag 300 320
3900 mark G_ARROW_HELD
4000 up
4200 parkbr
4600 mark I_ARROW_RELEASED
